# Repository Scope Guard
# ===================================
# This file defines the BOUNDARIES of this repository.
# Before creating ANY files, verify alignment with this scope.

## Repository Identity
REPO_NAME: Demo4AISupChn
PURPOSE: AI Supervision Command Center - Interactive UI/UX Demonstration
TYPE: Static Website / HTML Prototype / GitHub Pages Deployment

## Allowed Content Types
ACCEPTABLE_FILES:
  - *.html (web pages)
  - *.css (stylesheets)  
  - *.js (frontend JavaScript)
  - *.json (configuration/data)
  - *.png, *.jpg, *.gif, *.svg (images/screenshots)
  - *.md (documentation/README only)

## Forbidden Content Types (VIOLATIONS)
BLOCKED_FILES:
  - *.docx (Word documents - WRONG REPO!)
  - *.xlsx (Excel spreadsheets - WRONG REPO!)
  - *.pptx (PowerPoint presentations - WRONG REPO!)
  - Business documents of ANY kind
  - Email templates
  - Investor lists
  - Fundraising materials
  - Contract templates
  - Reports unrelated to AI demo

## Correct Locations for Other Document Types
BUSINESS_DOCS_REPO: ~/business-docs/ or separate dedicated repository
EMAIL_TEMPLATES: Should be in CRM/Outreach tooling repository
INVESTOR_LISTS: Should be in BD/Sales enablement repository
CODE_PROJECTS: Should have their OWN repositories

## Pre-Action Checklist (MUST VERIFY BEFORE CREATING FILES)
1. [ ] What is this repository FOR? (Check PURPOSE above)
2. [ ] Does this file match ACCEPTABLE_FILES list?
3. [ ] Am I putting business docs in an AI demo project? → STOP!
4. [ ] Would this file confuse someone who clones this repo?
5. [ ] Is there a BETTER location for this content?

## Emergency Procedures
IF SCOPE VIOLATION DETECTED:
1. STOP immediately - do not create more files
2. Move contaminated files to correct location
3. Git checkout -- . to restore clean state
4. Document what happened and why
5. Review session context for root cause

## Version History
CREATED: 2025-08-28
TRIGGER: Repository contamination incident - business docs created in AI demo repo
LESSON: Always verify repository scope before generating deliverables
